# PROJECT TITLE

Electromagnetism Virtual Laboratory: Interactive Electric and Magnetic Field Simulator

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior physics simulation engineer, electrical engineering educator, numerical computing specialist, 3D visualization developer, and Android application architect.

Develop a complete, interactive educational application that teaches electric and magnetic phenomena through mathematical calculations, animated field visualizations, and virtual experiments.

The application is intended for university-level electrical and electronic engineering students, physics students, laboratory demonstrations, and classroom teaching.

Its purpose is to help students understand how physical quantities behave when experimental parameters change.

Do not create merely an educational website, formula collection, static textbook, or animation gallery.

Create a working virtual laboratory in which students can manipulate physical parameters and immediately observe the resulting changes.

The application must explain the underlying physics and display the numerical results generated by the simulation.

